  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "A round of pale birchwood on a woven grass cord, given by Naldor the Green to those he takes up into the Green Listening -- the old Woodman craft of hearing the slow turning of leaf and root and beast. It is warm to the hand, and steadies the wearer's mind toward the wood."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "A round of pale birchwood on a cord of woven grass, worn smooth by handling. It is warm, as a living thing is warm, and quiets the mind of one who would hear the slow breathing of the world."
    }
  },
